Adjust volume to 100 ml with distilled water. With storage this forms a purple solution with a rusty brown precipitate 
that should be resuspended before use. This classic formulation was recently improved by T.W. Hill (FGN, this volume)</P>

<p><B>Vitamin Solution</B>
<p>Add 100 mg each of biotin, pyridoxin, thiamine, riboflavin (light sensitive), PABA (p-aminobenzoic acid), 
nicotinic acid to 100 ml water. Add 2 drops chloroform as preservative. Store in a dark bottle at 4°C.</P>

<P>&nbsp;</P>
